    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d721">

                <pb facs="1162" n="1146" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p1/pg1146"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">785.00/10–3151: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Embassy in the
                        United Kingdom </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d721-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-11-17T13:54:00-05:00">November 17,
                            1951—1:54 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2564. Re Embtel 2118 Oct 31. Dept has informed Brit Emb rep here <pb facs="1163"
                        n="1147" xml:id="pg1147"/> that our intelligence auths entirely agree with
                    estimate Brit mil intel concerning potential use Yalu dam as communications line
                    and that in discussions with Morrison this subject Sec had not been correctly
                    briefed. However, we pointed out as also stated by Sec to Morrison, dam is very
                    important source electric power for Port Arthur, Dairen industrial and military
                    complex.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d721-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d721-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram, drafted by U. Alexis Johnson, summarized the substance of a
                    conversation which he had held with Mr. Tomlinson of the British Embassy on the
                    preceding day.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
